{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) achieved only ~48.5% validation accuracy, a weak baseline that gives little signal about which design axis (modality, encoder, aggregation, fusion) will drive improvement. Uncertainty: The most critical open question is whether the image modality carries substantially more discriminative information than the RNA profile for this task. This experiment tests image_only with a strong pretrained encoder (resnet50) at the same singleprofile setting, providing a clean modality-level comparison against config_001. If image_only substantially outperforms 48.5%, it strongly justifies investing remaining budget in multimodal configurations; if it is comparable or worse, it signals that the bottleneck is representation quality (encoder choice) rather than modality, redirecting effort toward scvi/scgpt encoders. This is the highest-information single experiment at this stage because the modality decision gates the architecture of all subsequent multimodal experiments (configs 016-051) and determines where to focus the remaining 8 experiments."
}

